blitterbot 2026-10-26 19:59:52 +0000
FileSystemUtil: readAllText reads a file under three bytes (Refs #667, #1177)

skipUtf8Bom reads three bytes to look for a byte-order mark and seeks back
when there is none. On a file shorter than three bytes the read fails the
stream, and seekg on a failed stream does nothing, so readAllText and
readAllLines returned nothing for it: the offline achievements' export
holding one one-digit game id (two bytes, "7\n") read as no games ready.

The stream's state is cleared before the seek. A bug in upstream-carried
code, contained to the one line (es-code-traps.md, "A file under three
bytes"); the change is offered upstream with the fork's other fixes.

es-file-tests compiles the shipped FileSystemUtil.cpp now, with the four
things a read never reaches as stand-ins in FileSystemReadTests.cpp: the
1- and 2-byte files read as "" and readAllLines found no line before (3
assertions), and every size reads whole now, a BOM still skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


diff --git a/es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp b/es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp
index ba62f7e74..40cc13ec5 100644
--- a/es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp
@@ -1375,6 +1375,10 @@ namespace Utils
 			if (file.read(bom, 3) && bom[0] == '\xEF' && bom[1] == '\xBB' && bom[2] == '\xBF')			
 				return;
 			
+			// A file under three bytes failed the read above, and seekg does
+			// nothing on a failed stream: without the clear, such a file read
+			// as empty (pixelelated #1177).
+			file.clear();
 			file.seekg(0);
 		}
 
