blitterbot 2026-10-27 00:58:11 +0000
es-core: a download replaces its target only after the whole artifact arrived, and renameFile fails on an absent source (Refs #668, #1191)

- es-core/src/utils/DownloadFile.{h,cpp}: a file-mode download's start
  (a temporary of its own, <path>.tmp.<pid>.<n>, the target untouched),
  its close (the flush's and the close's results) and its finish (the
  temporary over the target only when the stream closed cleanly and
  the temporary is there; otherwise it is removed).
- es-core/src/HttpReq.{h,cpp}: uses them; a failed flush or close is
  mStreamFailed; the destination is no longer removed at the start.
- es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp: renameFile returns false for an
  absent source and, on POSIX, no longer removes the destination before
  rename(2).
- es-app/tests/unit: es-fs-tests (FileSystemTests.cpp), six of its eight
  cases failing on the pin's behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


diff --git a/es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp b/es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp
index ba62f7e74..27f93d91b 100644
--- a/es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/utils/FileSystemUtil.cpp
@@ -1447,19 +1447,24 @@ namespace Utils
 
 		bool renameFile(const std::string& src, const std::string& dst, bool overWrite)
 		{
-			std::string path = getGenericPath(src);			
+			std::string path = getGenericPath(src);
+			// Nothing to move is a failure (T21 PL-04, #1191): it answered
+			// true, and a download whose temporary was gone was called done.
 			if (!exists(path, false))
-				return true;
-
-			if (overWrite && exists(dst, false))
-				removeFile(dst);
+				return false;
 
 			FileCache::remove(path);
 			FileCache::remove(dst);
 
-#if WIN32			
+#if WIN32
+			if (overWrite && exists(dst, false))
+				removeFile(dst);
+
 			return MoveFileW(Utils::String::convertToWideString(path).c_str(), Utils::String::convertToWideString(dst).c_str());
 #else
+			// rename(2) replaces an existing destination in one step; removing
+			// it first left a moment with neither file (T21 PL-04, #1191).
+			(void) overWrite;
 			return std::rename(src.c_str(), dst.c_str()) == 0;
 #endif
 		}
