blitterbot 2026-10-27 11:10:10 +0000
es-app, es-core: the cloud pages read a command's whole output, parse a status once, and quote through one function (Refs #673, #1225)

T26 PL-11:
- Utils::Platform::GetShOutput (es-core) cut the last byte off every
  fgets chunk: the newline of a short line, but a real character of each
  255-byte piece of a long one and of a last line with no newline; and it
  read from popen's result without testing it. It now drops only a
  newline -- its callers' contract, the lines joined without them, is
  kept -- and a command that cannot start gives "". A contained fix of
  es-core's code under bugs-are-agent-first.md rule 6, a #585 line.
- A cloud_remote change's "OK=<name>" was parsed two ways over the
  joined text: anywhere in it (create), at its start (select, remove),
  and the name could run on into the next line. The changes are read
  whole (cloudRemoteRun: every line and the exit status; not
  executeScriptLegacy, which echoes each line to stdout unmasked, where a
  create's credentials could land), and success is a whole "OK=<name>"
  line with a zero exit (cloudRemoteOkName), in one place.
- FINISH RESTORE PROCESS's CHECK CONNECTION read an empty `echo $?` as 0,
  YOUR CLOUD IS ANSWERING. An empty or garbled status is now a failure
  (cloudExitStatus), which says the not-answering sentence.

T26 PL-21: cloudShellQuote was es-core's Utils::String::shellQuote under
another name. tests/shell-quote-equality.py showed them byte-equal over
20 values (quotes, $( ), backticks, backslashes, newlines, UTF-8, the
empty string) first, and fires on a copy one character off; then the 16
call sites moved to shellQuote and the copy went. The test now checks
that the shell gives every value back through shellQuote.
credential-quoting: 8 sites, 8 quoted, as before.

tests/command-readers.py runs the extracted GetShOutput against real
commands and a failed popen, and the extracted parse and status reader
over their cases: FAIL at 16dbac521 on all five points (a 300-byte line
back as 299, CONNECTE, a crash on the failed popen, two parses, atoi),
PASS here, and FAIL on two constructed copies. cloud-set-systems-quoting
and cloud-content-selection extract the one quoting function now: 5 of
5 and 14 of 14, at the pin and here.

Already written: nothing -- reads, parses and quoting; no stored state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


